  "2026-11-07T02:13:39.648Z",codex-agent,"Resumed review round after clean status and existing receipts check. Fresh remote main was one commit ahead; merge it before fixes. Two unresolved findings are valid: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60w0W6 (null direct contract metadata shadows valid nested metadata) and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60vzXu (contract summary title bypasses single-line normalization). General rules: nullish compatibility projections must fall back without discarding auditable standalone malformed values; line-oriented output normalizes every projected title through the same presentation policy. Search the whole package and exercise SDK, CLI, JSON/TOON, snapshots and packed Node/Bun consumers in synthetic non-git fixtures. Preserve previous regression tests and prove only new behavioral reverts in disposable copies."
  "2026-11-07T02:22:30.524Z",codex-agent,"Class search completed across src, scripts, tests and public CLI/SDK projections. readContractChange is the sole contract source-precedence reader; all consumers already share it. Fix nullish fallback while preserving standalone null and malformed non-null direct values, including undefined-direct/nested-null history. getStringField already validates before metadata fallback; additive breaking flags and audience declarations have distinct existing contracts and are unchanged. Route summary and JSON titles through resolveEntryTitle, keep neutral closure first and explicit declaration titles ahead of close_reason, and normalize the final summary line to bound caller-supplied heading/version/category/title/id. Baseline: all 3 new adversarial tests failed. Fixed: 13/13 contract tests passed, including 90 precedence pairs through JSON/TOON round trips, 100 seeded titles across 8 grouping/entry-source combinations, and real offline npm-packed Node/Bun SDK/CLI/host consumers using synthetic non-git trackers. Prior neutral-JSON assertions were strengthened rather than weakened."
  "2026-11-07T02:23:38.778Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node scripts/prove-contract-changes-revert.ts passed all 14 fixed-pass / behavioral-revert-fail / restored-pass cases in a disposable copy. Five new independent reverts cover PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60w0W6 (restore undefined-only precedence), PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60vzXu (restore raw summary titles), the matching raw JSON-title bypass, removal of shared declared-title/entry-source policy, and removal of final one-line formatting. Each reverted behavior fails its adversarial property test with ERR_ASSERTION and passes again after restoration. The previous nine revert cases remain passing after the shared title refactor and main merge; neutral JSON now also asserts absence of contract metadata. No existing test was deleted or weakened. Full release gates will be attempted serially with at most two workers and a combined local time budget, preserving all thresholds."
