  "2026-11-07T14:04:12.940Z",codex-agent,"Final current-source results: focused publication/contract/claim suite 27/27 and broader 17-file targeted suite 577/577, zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 16 independent behavioral revert cases passed fixed/reverted/restored assertions. The 5760-case publication oracle covers hidden=1376, published=2464, excluded=1920 configurations and verifies ordinary gaps remain; packed Node/Bun consumers verify the incomplete neutral issue through SDK, CLI/raw input/frozen snapshots and extension host in JSON/TOON. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstrings (266 declarations, 42 files), zero-vulnerability production audit, both 111-file package checks, changelog/link and release date/attestation gates pass. No thresholds or dependency pins changed. Full npm/Bun gates for this head remain for CI under the original local-runtime condition: the prior measured pair exhausted one hour and did not complete Bun. Prior-head full results are not claimed as certification for this head. Both current findings are fixed with one shared eligibility policy; no findings refused, no thread replies/resolutions, no PR merge/release. Release own claim and retain in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-09T11:53:52.927Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: fetched all threads; three unresolved (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60xqLq claim-audit, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6022qh contract-changes:29, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6022qj generator:651) plus the latest CodeRabbit pre-merge linked-issues failure: render declared contract changes for neutral closed items under Changed (SDK contract) and audit their missing migration text. Plan: remove the neutral-closure gate from the shared contract presentation policy so every authored declaration of a rendered item publishes (Markdown, JSON, summary, audit); neutral Closed wording then applies only to undeclared closures; semver/breaking exclusion of unproven closures stays unchanged. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6022qj (summary formatter single-line bound) will be answered with evidence: undeclared pipeline output is byte-identical to main and the bound is the owner-confirmed fix for resolved thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60vzXu. Branch merged current origin/main first."
  "2026-11-09T12:01:05.862Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3 implementation: the shared contract presentation policy no longer suppresses authored declarations on unproven neutral closures. readContractChange is now the single presentation reader for Markdown, JSON, summary and audit (the separate eligibility wrapper is gone), and entry titles resolve the declaration before neutral closure wording, so a declared neutral item renders once under Changed (SDK contract) with its migration line and the audit reports missing migration text for its published placeholders, exactly as the linked-issues pre-merge check and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6022qh require. Unproven closures still never contribute to breaking or semver classification, and undeclared closures keep neutral Closed wording everywhere. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60xqLq's invariant (audit describes only published assertions) is preserved by the shared reader; its specific suggestion to skip migration gaps for neutral claims is superseded, because those claims now publish contract text and the remedy describes the rendered placeholder. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6022qj is refused with evidence: on main, resolveEntryTitle already single-lined every item-derived summary title, so undeclared items render byte-identically through the package pipeline and existing snapshots are unchanged; the formatSummaryLine bound only affects hand-constructed entries passed directly to the exported formatter, which is the owner-confirmed fix for resolved thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60vzXu ('the formatter bounds every caller-supplied field to one line') and its regression test fails on revert (summary formatter line boundary case)."
  "2026-11-09T12:01:11.440Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node scripts/prove-contract-changes-revert.ts passes 16 independent fixed-pass / behavioral-revert-fail / restored-pass cases in disposable copies. Seven cases cover this round's publish policy: re-introducing the neutral-closure gate independently in category grouping, field grouping, the Markdown bullet, the JSON projection, the entry-title precedence or the audit each fails the new declared-issues test with ERR_ASSERTION, and a second copy of source precedence in the audit (the nullish coalescing one-liner) fails the publication oracle. The previous nine cases (extension registration, field isolation, equal backtick runs, unmatched run recovery, nullish metadata precedence, summary/document title projection, shared entry-source policy, formatter line boundary) remain intact."
  "2026-11-09T12:17:54.519Z",codex-agent,"Continuation verified the existing branch, remote PR and append-only tracker; retained the main merge and valid uncommitted declaration-publishing fixes. Correction to the prior summary-formatter refusal: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6022qj is valid for the exported formatSummaryLine API because callers may construct undeclared entries directly. Scope line normalization to the reserved contract section and preserve exact historical formatting for all ordinary entries; add a regression and behavioral revert. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60xqLq requests an invariant that remains required, but its suggested neutral-closure suppression is superseded by issue 317 and the latest CodeRabbit linked-issue finding: declared neutral items now publish contract text, so their missing migration must be audited. The publication oracle and neutral-declaration regressions verify this correspondence. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Prior full-pair runtime exceeded the one-hour condition, so use current focused and package gates and let CI certify full npm/Bun without weakening thresholds."
  "2026-11-09T12:21:49.626Z",codex-agent,"Self-review refined summary compatibility: restore formatSummaryLine exactly to its historical behavior, including caller fields whose category happens to be the contract heading. Normalize only actual declarations during toSummaryEntry projection, where source metadata is available; never infer declaration status from headings. Tests cover ordinary caller fields with all line separators and whitespace, actual declaration title/id/version projection, all section groupings, neutral declared/undeclared closures, and unchanged ordinary evidence rules. Credential-free health with an isolated home passes the CI warning baseline: only the existing 32 legacy provenance events remain; the initial extension-version-skew warning came from the normal local home configuration. Execute pm linked-test runs in a scratch copy of the tracker to keep run artifacts out of the package tracker as required."
